Package: pg-loganalyze
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: PostgreSQL auto_explain log analyzer (TUI)
 A terminal user interface (TUI) application for analyzing PostgreSQL
 auto_explain extension logs. Provides interactive browsing of query plans,
 execution times, and performance statistics.
 .
 Features:
  * Parse and analyze PostgreSQL auto_explain logs
  * Interactive terminal interface for browsing results
  * Query plan visualization and analysis
  * Performance statistics aggregation
  * Support for compressed log files (gzip, bzip2)

Package: pg-loganalyze-exporter
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, systemd, adduser
Recommends: postgresql-common
Suggests: prometheus
Description: PostgreSQL auto_explain log analyzer (Prometheus exporter)
 A daemon service that continuously monitors PostgreSQL auto_explain logs
 and exports metrics to Prometheus. Includes state management, scheduling,
 and systemd integration for production deployments.
 .
 Features:
  * Continuous monitoring of PostgreSQL logs
  * Prometheus metrics export
  * State persistence with SQLite
  * Systemd service integration
  * Configurable polling intervals and retention
  * Support for multiple log file patterns
 .
 This package creates a 'pg-exporter' system user and provides systemd
 service configuration for automatic startup and management.